A back-valued correction cannot be written: a `txn` block, `post`, `debit` and `credit` have no argument or clause for a posting's value date (the grammar's `Txn` is an idempotency key and a body), so the correction's legs can only take the default value date. The two reads — `.valid_at(v@2026-01-21)` and `.as_of(#5)` — are expressible (B02, B01); the write the task is about is not. SPEC-LANGUAGE §bitemporality records the axis as "Partial".
